Dockerfile Directives 

1. FROM – I use FROM to choose the base image.
👉 Example: FROM ubuntu:22.04
I start my Dockerfile with a base image.


2. LABEL – I use LABEL to add metadata about the image.
👉 Example: LABEL maintainer="venkat@example.com"
I mention who maintains this image.


3. ENV – I use ENV to set environment variables inside the container.
👉 Example: ENV APP_HOME=/usr/src/app
We set paths or configuration values.


4. RUN – I use RUN to execute commands while building the image.
👉 Example: RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y python3
We install packages or dependencies.


5. COPY – I use COPY to copy files from my computer to the container.
👉 Example: COPY . /app
I copy my project files inside the image.


6. ADD – I use ADD to add files or download URLs, or extract archives.
👉 Example: ADD app.tar.gz /app
I can also use it to unpack tar files.


7. WORKDIR – I use WORKDIR to set the working directory in the container.
👉 Example: WORKDIR /app
We don’t need to use cd again.


8. EXPOSE – I use EXPOSE to inform Docker which port the app will use.
👉 Example: EXPOSE 8080
I expose the port my application runs on.


9. USER – I use USER to set the user who runs the container.
👉 Example: USER node
We avoid running as root for security.


10. CMD – I use CMD to set the default command when the container starts.
👉 Example: CMD ["python3", "app.py"]
I define the main process for the container.


11. ENTRYPOINT – I use ENTRYPOINT to force a specific command to run.
👉 Example: ENTRYPOINT ["python3", "app.py"]
We can still add extra arguments at runtime.


12. VOLUME – I use VOLUME to store data outside the container.
👉 Example: VOLUME /data
We keep data safe even if the container stops.


13. ARG – I use ARG to set build-time variables.
👉 Example: ARG VERSION=1.0
I can pass custom values during build.


14. HEALTHCHECK – I use HEALTHCHECK to check if the app is healthy.
👉 Example: HEALTHCHECK CMD curl -f http://localhost:8080 || exit 1
We monitor the container’s health.


15. SHELL – I use SHELL to change the default shell for RUN commands.
👉 Example: SHELL ["/bin/bash", "-c"]
We use bash instead of sh if needed.


16. ONBUILD – I use ONBUILD to add triggers for child images.
👉 Example: ONBUILD COPY . /app
We use this for base images that others will extend.


17. STOPSIGNAL – I use STOPSIGNAL to define how the container stops.
👉 Example: STOPSIGNAL SIGTERM
I tell Docker what signal to send when stopping.
